[Reply to joseph@milo.amd.com, I am using a friend's account]

The new Nethack version is much improved, and is still
in my opinion THE BEST COMPUTER GAME, bar none.

There is only one huge problem with the new version...
It is WAY TOO EASY.

In version 3.0 my median score, equally weighting all character
classes, was about 3,000 points.  ( From 3 tournaments --
Each tournament consisted of 24 games, 2 per character class, 
played over a 48 hour period.)  With the new version I
believe my median score will be much, much higher.

The first game I played, I easily made over 20,000 points
and only died while trying to find out if I could be
killed.  A few games later I made over 200,000 points
without much effort.  The gnomish mines offer easy
experience points and little danger.

This detracts from my joy of playing.  My sence of
accomplishment seems hollow because it was too easy.  When I 
have a great game and want to brag to my friends, they
don't care because they are doing just as well.  The element
of fear which is one the best things about nethack (Wizardry
and Ultima lack it) has been reduced.

Another problem with the games being easier, is that the
average game takes too long to play.  I don't want to play
most games for several hours!

In a previously posted article, someone complained about
having a 70 hit point character killed by a gnome with
a wand of sleep.  If this happened to me, I would love it.
If friends were watching they could laugh at me, and if
I was alone I would have a great hack story.  (all great
hack stories end with death.)


Suggestion:

This problem could be fixed by having multiple levels of
difficulty, each having its own high score list.  This would
accommodate all tastes.


